config TYPEC_SM5714
	tristate "Silicon Mitus SM5714 Type-C Port Controller"
	depends on I2C
	depends on TYPEC_TCPM
	help
	  A USB Type-C Port Controller (tcpc_dev) driver for the Silicon Mitus
	  SM5714 PMIC's autonomous Type-C/PD controller (PDIC), binding it to the
	  kernel's USB-PD policy engine (tcpm).  The SM5714 has a vendor register
	  layout rather than a standard TCPCI block, so it is integrated the way
	  Qualcomm's PMIC Type-C is: this driver provides the CC/role/PD-FIFO
	  transport and feeds tcpm's state machine from the chip interrupt.

	  Say Y or M here to use USB-PD on boards with the SM5714 (e.g. the
	  Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra, SM-X910).
